Problem: Given real numbers \( m, n, p, M \) satisfy:
$$
M=\frac{m}{n+p}=\frac{n}{p+m}=\frac{p}{m+n},
$$
what is the value of \( M \)?
(A) -1
(B) \(\frac{1}{2}\)
(C) 1
(D) \(\frac{1}{2}\) or -1

Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{}.<|im_end|>
